DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppaamm__ggeetteennvvlliisstt() function returns a copy of the given PAM context's
     environment list as a pointer to an array of strings.  The last element
     in the array is NULL.  The pointer is suitable for assignment to _e_n_v_i_r_o_n.

     The array and the strings it lists are allocated using malloc(3), and
     should be released using free(3) after use:

         char **envlist, **env;

         envlist = environ;
         environ = pam_getenvlist(pamh);
         /* do something nifty */
         for (env = environ; *env != NULL; env++)
             free(*env);
         free(environ);
         environ = envlist;

